# Financial market data pipeline

Version: 0.1
Status: Draft

## Project Objective 
An end-to-end stock market analysis pipeline for automated retrieval, validation, and storage for analytical application

## 1. Functional requirements
FR-01	The system shall retrieve historical stock market data from an external API.
FR-02	The system shall extract opening, closing, high, low, and volume values.
FR-03	The system shall validate incoming market data.
FR-04	The system shall store validated records in a relational database.
FR-05	The system shall prevent duplicate records.
FR-06	The system shall support automated data updates.
FR-07	The system shall display analytical results through an interactive interface.

## 2. Nonfunctional requirements
NFR-01	The system shall store API credentials securely outside the source code.
NFR-02	The system shall log ingestion errors.
NFR-03	The source code shall support independent testing of core components.
NFR-04	The application shall provide reproducible installation instructions.

ING-NFR-01	API credentials shall not be hardcoded or logged.
ING-NFR-03	HTTP requests shall have a configurable timeout.
ING-NFR-04	Core functions shall be independently testable.
ING-NFR-05	Function names, parameters and return values shall be documented.


## 3. Technology Stack

- Python 3.12
- PostgreSQL
- REST API
- SQL
- Git and GitHub
- Jupyter Notebook
- Dash

## 4. Scope Limitations

Version 1.0 will focus on historical equities data.

The following features are outside the initial scope:

- Real-time market streaming
- Options pricing
- Automated trading
- Machine learning predictions
- Advanced backtesting

## 5. Misc. details- 

- ETL = extract, transform, load
- JSON = JavaScript Object Notation